# Copy catalog sync

## Code catalog (`src/copy/catalog.ts`)
When adding or changing **user-facing text** in the UI, add a key + default in the catalog and render with `useT()` / `t('…')` - do not leave a hardcoded string in the component.

## Settings → Copy (`COPY_SETTINGS_KEYS`)
Only list **example / placeholder** strings there (e.g. `form.*.placeholder*`, `search.placeholder`).

Do **not** put in Settings → Copy:
- Basic chrome: nav, home title, empty-state CTAs, “Back to shows”
- Obvious section labels: Produced By, Starring, Genre, etc.
- Singular/plural pairs (e.g. Special Guest / Special Guests) - keep both in the catalog for code; only edit via code defaults

When adding a new **example** placeholder to the UI, add it to both `COPY_CATALOG` and `COPY_SETTINGS_KEYS`. When adding a basic label, catalog only.

Exceptions: brand name, tagline, and home title/subtitles are edited on **Branding** (not Copy). Do not add hints unless explicitly asked.
